    "switches": {
      "ownrows": [
        "| `LAMP_OWN_KEYS` (`lamp-setup`, `lamp-cloud`, `lamp-voice`) | `on`; the product's three units set it on (#2846), effective immediately when installed, with no runtime acceptance gate (the code's default is off: a unit without it reads no person's key); the voice's unit also loads the keys' folder (`LoadCredential=own:/etc/lampOS/voice/own`, made by `ConfigurationDirectory=`); in `lamp-cloud` also with `LAMP_CLOUD` and `LAMP_SETTINGS_CHANGE`, which the product already sets on, so enabling own keys also opens the app's `keys.*` calls; the keys helper's units are in `install`'s list, the socket enabled. A person's own DeepSeek endpoint and key and Deepgram key, at setup or from the app, each checked once before it is kept in root's folder; the second route's chat and speech use them, else the relay, and a key later refused goes back to the relay with `lamp-health`'s `voice-keys` warning. Off on all three units: setup keeps nothing, the app's kinds are \"not on this lamp\", and the voice reads no person's key. A retained voice-only off override leaves setup and app key storage on, while the voice ignores those keys (own-keys.md) | \u2014 | on in the product units (#2846; pinned by install.rs) | #2167 (#2094) | Historical drop-in trial on 22 Oct (#2845, #2861): setup keys worked and file modes/journal checks were recorded. That is not current-head acceptance. Owed: fresh install with no key keeps the relay; app set/remove/get with current settings on; keys remain in use after a full update; broker/account/TLS acceptance (#2094) | Merge prerequisite: explicit acceptance on the activation PR for #2094 and a fresh current-base lamp check; the PR stays HOLD until then, not the installed units | A person's keys send conversations to their chosen provider; settings is already on, so this change also opens the app calls. Installer tests alone do not qualify that activation | on |"
